+## Failed session setup
+
+- If `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the orchestrator awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with the original error, provided those hooks complete normally; both hooks receive the original session and `onError` receives the original error. Cleanup runs even after partial setup: `afterSession` must not assume setup completed or that user-input processing, a model response, or tool execution occurred, and deployers must track their own allocations to release only resources they acquired. ([validated by: reports a beforeSession failure and finishes cleanup before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
